Well, I'm not entirely sure about providers like `deepinfra`, but here is some info if you'd like to go forward with your change:
Changing the handler to something like this should work:
```ts
  const handleModelChange = (model: string) => {
    let newSettings = { ...settings, LLM_MODEL: model };

    if (settings.LLM_MODEL.split("/")[0] !== model.split("/")[0]) {
      newSettings = {
        ...newSettings,
        LLM_API_KEY: localStorage.getItem(`API_KEY_${model}`) || "",
      };
    }

    setSettings((prev) => ({ ...prev, ...newSettings }));
  };
```

Keep in mind the component actually calls `handleModelChange` on every keystroke. So unless the user directly pastes their desired model or selects it from the dropdown, they API key will reset (because the conditional always fails).

